## Later local activation

Python 3.12+ and uv are intended. After authorized runtime activation, resolve and
review dependencies and generate `uv.lock`, then use the following commands. These
are intended instructions, not evidence that they have succeeded:

```console
uv sync
uv run claim-auditor demo --offline --out results-local/demo-001
uv run claim-auditor verify-report results-local/demo-001/run
```

The demo creates owned source containing a declared function, an invented API and
an operational claim. Verdicts are generated through snapshot, inventory, index,
policy, citation and report services; no prerecorded verdict output is shipped.
Actual evidence and coverage are stored alongside `report.json`, Markdown and
escaped static HTML. A later tamper exercise must show integrity refusal.

For an existing complete local Git object store, supply a full object ID:

```console
uv run claim-auditor snapshot --repo /path/to/local-repo --commit FULL_OBJECT_ID --out results-local/snapshot-001
uv run claim-auditor audit --snapshot results-local/snapshot-001 --readme README.md --mode rules --out results-local/audit-001
uv run claim-auditor verify-report results-local/audit-001
```

No target code or README commands are run. Worktree indirection, archives, shallow
or alternate/promisor object stores are outside the supported acquisition boundary;
an ordinary owned fixture source is also accepted with `snapshot --fixture PATH`.
Every output path must be new. CLI errors use nonzero status; a complete report
does not mean the repository is correct.

## Architecture

- `contracts`: strict wire records and source-derived identity helpers.
- `snapshot`, `index`, `patterns`: frozen bytes and bounded static propositions.
- `inventory`: CommonMark block accounting and exact original-byte claims.
- `citations`: sole span/coverage reopening and report-integrity service.
- `audit`: deterministic negation-aware verdict reduction and run lifecycle.
- `report`: local JSON/JSONL, Markdown and inert HTML; owned demo inputs.
- `evaluation`: source-only packet preparation, one-to-one matching and scorer.
- `providers`, `screen`, `accounting`: explicit replay/disabled-live boundary,
  conservative model-input hold and bounded durable reservation port.

W2 adds typed fake/replay extraction and single-pass proposal source, paired-arm
orchestration, DEV-only annotation packages and append-only ruling operations.
These paths have **not run**. New CLI entrypoints for later authorized activation:

```console
uv run claim-auditor paired-run --packet results-local/prepared/packet.json --snapshot results-local/snapshot-001 --config paired-input.json --out results-local/paired-001
uv run claim-auditor paired-verify --run results-local/paired-001 --snapshot results-local/snapshot-001 --manifest-digest EXTERNALLY_PINNED_PAIRED_SHA256
uv run claim-auditor paired-score --run results-local/paired-001 --snapshot results-local/snapshot-001 --gold operator-gold.jsonl --out results-local/paired-score-001 --manifest-digest EXTERNALLY_PINNED_PAIRED_SHA256
uv run claim-auditor annotation-package --run results-local/audit-001 --family-id dev-example --out results-local/annotation-001
uv run claim-auditor rulings-import --ledger results-local/rulings.jsonl --input operator-rulings.jsonl
uv run claim-auditor rulings-export --ledger results-local/rulings.jsonl --out results-local/rulings-export.jsonl
```

`paired-input.json` must follow closed `PairedRunConfig`; it provides both fake
fixture arms or explicit relative replay paths, declared caps and prompt/model
identities. See [provider modes](docs/provider-modes.md). `paired-run` returns 3
because fake/replay assembly cannot complete actual comparative acceptance.
Fixture usage is simulated; live observations remain unknown. Annotation packages
contain source and blank review instructions, with no prepopulated human judgments.
Human imports additionally require the operator's `--confirm-human-action` after
actual human review with explicit action IDs. Agent judgments never become human
gold; importing records does not establish correctness or consensus.

`paired-verify` checks closed paired artifacts and admitted citations. Without an
external `--manifest-digest`, verification establishes internal consistency only.
`paired-score` verifies before opening separately supplied labels, preserves each
arm and requires fresh output. It supports one snapshot/family per run; no labels
are inputs to inference. Neither command is evidence of a live/human benchmark.

